      "hints": [
        "Complete the square: $2(x^2 - 6x) + 11 = 2[(x - 3)^2 - 9] + 11 = 2(x - 3)^2 - 7$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Factor out $2$ from the first two terms and complete the square:\n$$2x^2 - 12x + 11 = 2(x^2 - 6x) + 11 = 2\\left[(x - 3)^2 - 9\\right] + 11$$\n$$= 2(x - 3)^2 - 18 + 11 = 2(x - 3)^2 - 7$$\nwhere $a = 2, b = -3, c = -7$."
      ],
      "checking": {
